From: cwriter <https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/31313>
Subject: [PATCH] SYCL: lightning indexer VEC and XMX optimization (PR 31313, draft)

PR commit 11e34732 ("WIP K1: faster SYCL lightning indexer kernels", draft),
without its fused-gemm.cpp deduplication. The PR moves fused-gemm.cpp's
joint_matrix element traits, combination list and picker into a new xmx.hpp
under xmx_* names and makes fused-gemm.cpp use it. Here xmx.hpp is added for
the indexer only and fused-gemm.cpp keeps its own fg_* copy, because local
0010 and 0017 and candidates C20/C21 edit that code. The names do not overlap,
so both copies build side by side. Dropped with the dedup: the common.hpp
comment that points GGML_SYCL_XMX_GATHER_SHAPES at xmx.hpp and the docs rename
of the logged picker to xmx_pick_combo (fused-gemm.cpp still logs
fg_pick_combo). The PR's trailing blank line at the end of xmx.hpp is trimmed.

Vector kernels for F32/F16/BF16 keys and, for batches of 8+ tokens, a
joint_matrix kernel that uses the device's listed combinations (sub-group 8
8x8x16 on Xe-HPG / Arc A-series). DeepSeek-V3.2-style sparse attention.
Off by default: GGML_SYCL_LIGHTNING_INDEXER=1 turns it on;
GGML_SYCL_LIGHTNING_INDEXER_XMX_TYPES / _XMX_SHAPES restrict the XMX path.

